Z||000000||DaveL||05-10-2001||07:48 AM||||I recently put in a new set of 4X10's in the dash, and they are a great improvement over the old factory speakers. But now the right channel is much quieter than the left one. I've tries reversing the leads with no real change. Sound like a phase problem?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||05-10-2001||11:00 AM||||Real dumb question, I know, but have you checked your balance control?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-10-2001||01:58 PM||||Could there be something touching the cone of the quieter speaker, insulation or padding or something?<P> Could you have warped the speaker frame when you bolted it in, the speaker needs to be against a perfectly flat plane, not on a curved surface.<P>Could there be something between the speaker and the surface its bolted against? The lip of the speaker needs to be more or less airtight or the base response drops way off.<P>are you sure its not just that you are sitting on one side of the car, so the speaker closest to you sounds louder? That is normal.<P>  This is a stupid question: is your hearing normal? I lost 60dB of hearing sensitivity in my left ear when I was 33, and didnt even know it till I went for a routine physical.||||reg||1
